{"type":"message","id":"9eba8519","parentId":"1a3ec82d","timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:56:14.523Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the issue clearly. At 2026-06-04 01:06:57, the system opened a SHORT position on DOT:\n\n```\n开空 DOT @1.092 | 评分:70 | 状态:trending | AI:做多(65%)\nquantity_used: 183.2\n```\n\n183.2 DOT at 10x leverage at ~$1.092 price. Let me calculate:\n- 183.2 DOT × $1.092 ≈ $200 notional value\n- With 10x leverage, margin needed = $20 USDT\n\nThat's actually correct! 20 USDT margin at 10x = 200 USDT notional. DOT price ~1.092, so quantity = 200 / 1.092 ≈ 183.2.\n\nBut wait, the user says \"开仓金额不对\" (opening amount is wrong). Let me look at what the current position shows:\n\nLater at 08:00: `DOT LONG: entry=1.105, amount=11.7, current=1.107, pnl=+0.02`\n\nSo there's ANOTHER DOT position - a LONG at 1.105 with amount 11.7. But the system opened a SHORT at 1.092 with 183.2 quantity.\n\nSo there are TWO DOT positions? One SHORT at 1.092 (183.2 DOT) and one LONG at 1.105 (11.7 DOT)?\n\nThe SHORT has 183.2 DOT × 1.092 = $200 notional → $20 margin (correct for 10x)\nThe LONG has 11.7 DOT × 1.105 = $12.93 notional → $1.29 margin (way too small!)\n\nThis is the problem! The LONG position has only 11.7 DOT. At DOT price ~$1.105, that's only ~$13 notional, which is much less than the configured 20 USDT margin at 10x (= $200 notional).\n\nLet me look at what happened. The \"反转重建 DOT\" at 07:34 says \"API原始=11.7000 → 风控标准=181.0000\" - the API returned 11.7000 which seems to be the QUANTITY from Binance (11.7 DOT in the LONG position), and it was \"reversed\" to 181.0000. This looks like some data transformation issue.\n\nActually wait. Let me re-read. The API returned 11.7000. The system \"reversed\" it to 181.0. That doesn't make sense. But the SHORT position was opened with 183.2 quantity - close to the \"reversed\" value.\n\nHmm, let me think about this more carefully. The positions:\n1. A SHORT opened at 01:06:57 with 183.2 DOT (correct notional ~$200)\n2. A LONG showing at 08:00 with 11.7 DOT and entry 1.105\n\nThe 11.7 DOT position at entry 1.105 is the problematic one. At current DOT price of ~$1.10, 11.7 DOT is only ~$13 notional value, not the standard $200.\n\nI need to look at broader context around when the LONG position was opened. Let me search for it.\n\nActually, it could also be from earlier. Let me also check whether the system opened this LONG position or if it was manually opened. Let me search for \"DOT\" and \"LONG\" entries.\n\nLet me also look at the script to understand the \"反转重建\" (reverse rebuild) logic. The 11.7000 → 181.0000 transformation looks suspicious.\n\nBut actually, the main problem the user is reporting is \"开仓金额不对\" - the opening amount is wrong. Looking at the data:\n\nSHORT: 183.2 DOT @ 1.092 = ~$200 notional ✓ (correct, 20 USDT margin × 10x)\nLONG: 11.7 DOT @ 1.105 = ~$12.93 notional ✗ (wrong, should be $200)\n\nThe LONG position has only 11.7 DOT. This is way too small. The issue seems to be that a LONG position was opened with only ~$13 notional instead of $200.\n\nBut actually, I'm now looking at \"反转重建 DOT：API原始=11.7000 → 风控标准=181.0000\" more carefully. This might be a data parsing bug where the API returns quantity=11.7 and the code interprets it as price=11.7 in some transformation. Let me look at the code.\n\nWait - \"API原始=11.7000\" - what is this API value? It could be the position quantity from Binance API (11.7 DOT), and then \"风控标准=181.0000\" is some transformed value. The position quantity from the Binance API for the LONG is indeed 11.7 DOT.\n\nHmm, but the 11.7 DOT position: is this even a real position or is it a phantom? Let me check if there was a LONG position opened recently.\n\nLet me search for DOT LONG opening events.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_wFzyXMcXRfSQodGguEb65385","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -i \"DOT\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2