{"type":"message","id":"1a8d4ce4","parentId":"5b4afc38","timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:56:27.536Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so I see the issue more clearly now. Let me trace the history:\n\n1. There's a DOT LONG position that has been held since at least June 3rd: `entry=1.118, amount=11.7`. This is a very small position - only 11.7 DOT, which at $1.12 is only about $13 notional value. This is wrong - it should be $200 notional.\n\n2. On June 4 at 01:06:57, the system opened a new SHORT position on DOT with 183.2 DOT quantity - which is the correct size (~$200 notional at 10x = $20 margin).\n\n3. The \"反转重建\" (reverse rebuild) log entries show: \"API原始=11.7000 → 风控标准=181.0000\" - The system is getting 11.7 from the API (which appears to be the original LONG position's quantity), and then \"rebuilding\" it to 181.0 (which is roughly correct for the risk-control standard). But the actual position quantity remains 11.7.\n\nSo the problem is the LONG position with only 11.7 DOT. This was probably opened at the wrong amount. Let me look at when this LONG was originally opened.\n\nLet me search earlier in the logs to find when DOT was first opened as LONG. The earliest reference I see is June 3 at 10:01. Let me search further back.\n\nActually wait - the user's complaint is specifically about \"开仓金额不对\" (opening amount is wrong). Let me check the June 3 logs around when this position was opened.\n\nLet me also check whether this 11.7 DOT position was manually opened or opened by the monitor. The correct amount should be:\n- 20 USDT margin × 10x leverage = 200 USDT notional\n- 200 / DOT_price ≈ 200 / 1.12 ≈ 178.6 DOT\n\nSo the position should be ~179 DOT, not 11.7 DOT. 11.7 DOT is about 1/15th of what it should be.\n\nLet me check when this position was opened.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_cuQodQpuVI86wgZWUAbu7617","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -i \"DOT.*开多\\|DOT.*LONG.