{"type":"message","id":"4eaba614","parentId":"4934371a","timestamp":"2026-06-04T01:00:46.272Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me read the positions file and also look at the show_positions code to understand the full picture. Then let me fix the code. Let me think about what to fix.\n\nLooking at line 1842 issue: when the API returns a position with amount=11.7 and the local cache has been corrected to 181.0, the code uses 11.7. The P&L calculation with the wrong amount would be wrong, but actually the P&L would be calculated using unrealized_pnl from the API (which is accurate for the actual 11.7 position).\n\nActually wait, looking at the code flow more carefully:\n\n```python\nif api_pos:\n    amount = abs(float(api_pos.get(\"amount\", 0) or 0)) or amount\n    if api_pos.get(\"unrealized_pnl\") is not None and amount > 0:\n        unrealized_pnl = float(api_pos[\"unrealized_pnl\"])\n        # uses API's unrealized_pnl which is correct for 11.7 DOT\n```\n\nSo even with 11.7 DOT amount, the unrealized_pnl from API is correct. The display is accurate for what's actually on the exchange.\n\nBut the user is concerned about the \"开仓金额\" (opening amount) being wrong. They want the position to have the correct amount (~$200 notional).\n\nOK, I think the user wants me to:\n1. Fix whatever code bug caused the wrong amount\n2. The display issue is secondary\n\nActually, I just realized - maybe the issue is more recent. Let me check the current positions JSON to see what's actually saved there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_BhyHM9ugXqxopRcg9vAu2189","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_positions.json 2>/dev/null | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null | head -80","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":55,"output":782,"cacheRead":58240,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":59077,"cost":{"i