{"type":"message","id":"74e0b065","parentId":"07d6039d","timestamp":"2026-06-04T01:01:27.080Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, now I see the full picture:\n\nThe local positions file has:\n1. DOT LONG: entry=1.105, amount=181.0 (corrected by 反转重建)\n2. XRP SHORT: entry=1.187, amount=168.5 (correct, 168.5 × 1.187 ≈ $200)\n\nBut the API showed 2 positions earlier, and the DOT LONG has 11.7 on exchange. The local cache has 181.0.\n\nSo the display issue at line 1842 is:\n- Local cache says DOT has amount=181.0\n- API says DOT has amount=11.7\n- Code uses API's 11.7 for display and P&L\n\nThe question is: should the display use API amount or local amount? The API amount is the REAL position size. Using local amount would show inflated/fake P&L.\n\nBut actually, looking more carefully, the API's `unrealized_pnl` is correct for 11.7 DOT. So the P&L shown should be correct.\n\nNow, the user says \"开仓金额不对\" - opening amount is wrong. Maybe they're looking at the record/display and seeing 11.7 DOT instead of 181.0 DOT. The display code overriding local with API is hiding the \"expected\" amount.\n\nBut also, the user might want the ACTUAL position to be fixed. The 11.7 DOT LONG needs to be closed and re-opened with the correct size.\n\nLet me focus on fixing the code. I think there are two things to fix:\n\n1. **The display code (line 1842)**: Instead of blindly overriding `amount` with API value, we should use the local cached amount for display purposes, and get P&L from the API. This way the display shows the \"correct\" position sizing.\n\nActually no, that would show wrong P&L. Let me think again...\n\nThe P&L shown:\n- With API unrealized_pnl: accurate (based on actual 11.7 DOT)\n- With amount-based calculation: if we use 181.0 amount, P&L would be inflated 15x\n\nSo the display IS correct in showing the actual position state. The bug is not in the display.\n\nThe real bug is that the position itself was opened with wrong quantity. And the \"反转重建\" code at line 2342-2346 only fixes the LOCAL cache, not the actual position.\n\nLet me focus on what the user is actually asking me to fix. They said \"修复\" in response to my analysis. Let me look more carefully at what could be fixed in the code.\n\nLooking at the issues I identified:\n1. 5月29日反转重建时数量错误 → the code that caused this MIGHT have been fixed since (the 反转重建 code at line 2342 with `correct_amount`) \n2. Line 1842 overrides local amount with API amount → this is intentional and correct for P&L accuracy\n\nWait, maybe I should look at the FLOW more carefully. When does \"反转重建\" happen? Let me trace through the sync code.\n\n```python\n# Line 2342-2358\nif need_rebuild:\n    new_positions = []\n    for p in api_positions:\n        amt = float(p.get('amount', 0))\n        if amt != 0:\n            symbol = p['symbol']\n            entry = float(p.get('entry_price', 0))\n            size_pct = CONFIG[\"position_size_pct\"]\n            expected_qty = (CONFIG[\"total_capital\"] * size_pct * 10) / entry\n            correct_amount = format_quantity(symbol, expected_qty, entry)\n            log.info(f\"🔧 反转重建 {symbol}：API原始={abs(amt):.4f} → 风控标准={correct_amount:.4f}\")\n            ...\n            new_positions.append({\n                'amount': correct_amount,\n                ...\n            })\n    positions = new_positions\n    save_positions(positions)\n```\n\nAfter this, the local cache has correct_amount. But the exchange position is still the original (wrong) amount.\n\nThen when the hourly display runs, it reads API positions AND the local cache. The API amount (11.7) overrides the local (181.0).\n\nOK so the actual code flow works like this:\n1. Positions are read from local cache (with corrected amounts)\n2. API positions are fetched\n3. For display, API amounts override local amounts → shows 11.7\n4. P&L from API is used (correct for 11.7)\n\nThe user sees 11.7 in the display and thinks the opening amount is wrong. But actually the display is showing the REAL position size on the exchange.\n\nOK, I think the user wants me to fix the bug that CAUSES the wrong amount. That bug was likely in the position rebuild code BEFORE it was fixed. Let me check if the current code would correctly handle a position rebuild.\n\nActually, looking at the current code at line 2342-2358, it already has the fix:\n```python\n# 🐛 修复：反转重建持仓时按风控规则重算数量，不用 API 的 abs(amt)\nsize_pct = CONFIG[\"position_size_pct\"]\nexpected_qty = (CONFIG[\"total_capital\"] * size_pct * 10) / entry\ncorrect_amount = format_quantity(symbol, expected_qty, entry)\n```\n\nSo the fix for future rebuilds is already in place. The problem is the historical position (opened before the fix).\n\nBut maybe there are other issues. Let me look at what could still be wrong:\n1. The display showing API amount instead of local amount makes it look like the position has wrong size\n2. The position on the exchange needs to be closed and re-opened\n\nLet me look at the display code and see if I should fix it to NOT override the local amount with API amount. Actually, the display code OVERRIDES amount with API amount, which means:\n- If local cache says 181.0 (corrected), display shows 11.7 (API) → confusing\n- P&L from API is correct for 11.7 DOT\n\nThe fix should be: use API amount for P&L but display the local amount (which represents what the system EXPECTS the position to be).\n\nActually, that's also confusing. Let me think about what would be MOST HELPFUL to the user.\n\nThe user wants to see:\n1. The position they think they have (should be ~182 DOT)\n2. The actual P&L (which is correct from API)\n\nBut if we show \"amount=182 DOT\" and a P&L of -$0.02, that doesn't make sense either because 182 DOT should have a much larger P&L.\n\nOK I think the best approach is:\n1. Keep displaying the API amount (actual position size) - this is the ground truth\n2. But ALSO log a warning when there's a significant discrepancy between local expected amount and API actual amount\n3. Fix the actual issue: the position on the exchange\n\nThe fix for the current state: close the 11.7 DOT LONG and re-open with correct amount. But that's an operational action, not a code fix.\n\nWait, maybe the user just wants me to fix the code so it doesn't happen again. Let me look at what specifically could be fixed:\n\n1. Add a discrepancy detection in the sync/display code\n2. Make sure the new position opening always uses the correct formula (it already does)\n3. Maybe fix the display to show both expected and actual amounts\n\nActually, let me look at the code one more time. The issue at line 1842 is that it replaces the local `amount` variable with the API amount. But it still uses the API's `unrealized_pnl` for P&L. The amount is only used as fallback for P&L calculation when unrealized_pnl is not available.\n\nSo the fix for the display code could be: don't override `amount` with API amount for DISPLAY purposes. Instead, use it only when needed for P&L calculation. But this would make the display inconsistent with reality.\n\nHmm, I think the cleanest fix is to flag the discrepancy. Let me look at what the user actually sees and what they want fixed.\n\nThe user said \"DOT的开仓金额不对\" and \"修复\". I'll:\n1. Fix the display to NOT override local amount with API amount (show the expected amount)\n2. Use API unrealized_pnl for P&L display (which is correct)\n3. Make sure the display works correctly either way\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the display code more carefully:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ScdTup0LRVTpyEYIBbcv8564","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","limit":60,"offset":1836}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":882,"output":3782,"cacheRead":58624,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":63288,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason