{"type":"message","id":"4ab7e531","parentId":"74e0b065","timestamp":"2026-06-04T01:01:27.239Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_ScdTup0LRVTpyEYIBbcv8564","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    for pos in positions:\n        normalize_position(pos)\n        symbol = pos['symbol']\n        pos_type = pos['type']\n        entry_price = float(pos.get('entry_price', 0) or 0)\n        amount = position_amount(pos)\n        api_pos = api_by_symbol.get(symbol, {})\n\n        if api_pos:\n            amount = abs(float(api_pos.get(\"amount\", 0) or 0)) or amount\n            if api_pos.get(\"unrealized_pnl\") is not None and amount > 0:\n                unrealized_pnl = float(api_pos[\"unrealized_pnl\"])\n                current_price = float(\n                    api_pos.get(\"current_price\") or api_pos.get(\"mark_price\") or 0\n                ) or prices.get(symbol, {}).get('price', entry_price)\n            else:\n                current_price = prices.get(symbol, {}).get('price', entry_price)\n                unrealized_pnl = (\n                    (current_price - entry_price) * amount\n                    if pos_type == 'LONG'\n                    else (entry_price - current_price) * amount\n                )\n        else:\n            current_price = prices.get(symbol, {}).get('price', entry_price)\n            unrealized_pnl = (\n                (current_price - entry_price) * amount\n                if pos_type == 'LONG'\n                else (entry_price - current_price) * amount\n            )\n\n        log.info(\n            f\"  📍 {symbol} {pos_type}: entry={entry_price}, amount={amount}, \"\n            f\"current={current_price}, pnl={unrealized_pnl:+.2f}\"\n        )\n\n        notional = entry_price * amount\n        pnl_pct = (unrealized_pnl / notional * 100) if notional > 0 else 0\n        \n        display_price = prices.get(symbol, {}).get(\"price\") or current_price\n        open_score = pos.get(\"score\", \"—\")\n        total_floating += unrealized_pnl\n        pos_lines.append(\n            f\"**{symbol}** {pos_type} | 开仓：${entry_price:,.2f} | \"\n            f\"现价：${display_price:,.2f} | 开仓评分：{open_score} | \"\n            f\"盈亏：${unrealized_pnl:+.2f} ({pnl_pct:+.2f}%)\"\n        )\n\n    # 构建所有币种的价格和评分列表\n    all_coins_lines = []\n\n    for symbol in CONFIG[\"symbols\"]:\n        if prices.get(symbol):\n            price = prices[symbol].get('price', 0)\n            change_24h = prices[symbol].get('change_24h', 0)\n            \n            ind = indicators.get(symbol, {})\n            regime = detect_regime(ind) if ind else \"ranging\"\n            fr = 0\n            score_txt = _format_hourly_score_line(\n                symbol, prices[symbol], ind, regime, fg, fr, btc_ind\n\n[765 more lines in file. Use offset=1896 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780534887218}}
{"type":"message","id":"ca7cda21","parentId":"4ab7e531","timestamp":"2026-06-04T01:01:49.960Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full picture. Looking at line 1842:\n\n```python\namount = abs(float(api_pos.get(\"amount\", 0) or 0)) or amount\n```\n\nThis overrides the local `amount` with the API amount. The issue is:\n1. Local cache has 181.0 (corrected by 反转重建)\n2. API has 11.7 (actual position on exchange)\n3. This overrides to 11.7, and the display shows 11.7\n\nAnd then `notional = entry_price * amount` is calculated with the overridden amount, and `pnl_pct = unrealized_pnl / notional * 100`.\n\nThe `unrealized_pnl` from API is correct for 11.7 DOT, and `notional = 1.105 * 11.7 ≈ 12.93`, so `pnl_pct = 0.02 / 12.93 ≈ 0.15%`.\n\nActually wait - looking at the log: `DOT LONG: entry=1.105, amount=11.7, current=1.107, pnl=+0.02`. The P&L of +$0.02 for 11.7 DOT at entry 1.105 and current 1.107: (1.107 - 1.105) * 11.7 = 0.002 * 11.7 = 0.0234 ≈ +0.02. That checks out.\n\nBut the user expects this position to be ~182 DOT, with P&L of ~$0.37. The wrong amount makes everything look tiny.\n\nOK here's my plan for the fix:\n\n1. **Display fix (line 1842)**: Don't override `amount` with API amount. Instead, keep the local amount (which has been normalized by 反转重建). This way the display shows the STANDARD position amount. But... the P&L will then be wrong if we multiply (price_diff * local_amount).\n\n2. **Better approach**: Use the local cached amount for display (showing the expected position size), and use the API `unrealized_pnl` for P&L.\n\nActually, the problem with approach 2 is that if the local amount is 181.0 but the actual P&L is $0.02 (for 11.7 DOT), showing `notional = 181.0 * 1.105 = $200` and `pnl% = 0.02/200 = 0.01%` would be misleading.\n\n3. **Best approach**: Show the local cached amount as the \"display amount\" but use API data for P&L/price. AND add a warning when API amount differs significantly from local amount.\n\nActually, I think the simplest and most correct fix is:\n- Remove the API amount override at line 1842\n- Keep using API `unrealized_pnl` for P&L (this is always correct)\n- Keep using local cached amount for display\n\nBut wait, if the local cached amount is 181.0 and the API unrealized_pnl is $0.02, then the `pnl_pct = unrealized_pnl / (entry_price * amount)` would show a tiny percentage (0.02/200 = 0.01%), which doesn't match the actual position. That's confusing.\n\nOK, let me think about this differently. Maybe the right fix is to add a DETECTION and WARNING when there's a discrepancy, rather than changing the display logic.\n\nActually, you know what, let me re-read the user's message: \"DOT的开仓金额不对老婆，又是哪里的代码出问题了\"\n\nThe user is saying \"DOT's opening amount is wrong, where in the code is the problem?\"\n\nThey want to know which code is causing the wrong amount. Let me identify:\n\n1. The positions.json has been corrected to 181.0 by 反转重建\n2. The display uses API amount (11.7) instead\n3. So the bug in the DISPLAY is at line 1842\n\nBut wait, the bigger issue: is 11.7 really the amount on the exchange? Let me verify by checking what Binance shows.\n\nActually, I should just check what the positions API shows. Let me run the position query.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_GnaerzhJptsDdDr76cT87520","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nfrom binance_auto_trade import get_all_positions\npositions = get_all_positions()\nif positions:\n    for p in positions:\n        sym = p.get('symbol','?')\n        amt = p.get('amount',0)\n        entry = p.get('entry_price',0)\n        pnl = p.get('unrealized_pnl',0)\n        print(f'{sym}: amount={amt}, entry={entry}, uPnl={pnl}')\nelse:\n    print('No positions or API failed')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":680,"output":2