{"type":"message","id":"3e8a17e2","parentId":"5a3c1516","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:42:20.614Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the problem clearly! Let me trace the timeline:\n\n1. We closed the DOT LONG (11.7 DOT) \n2. The monitor kept running (we didn't restart it)\n3. The monitor saw a signal and tried to open a DOT position\n4. It tried to close the \"position\" it thought existed (193.1 DOT from the local cache) with reduce_only → failed because the position was only 11.7 DOT on exchange\n5. It then fell back to a regular open order: `开空 数量=193.100000 @ $1.081000`\n6. But the ACTUAL position opened was only 11.7 DOT (not 193.1)\n\nWait, ACTUALLY: the current DOT amount is 11.7 at entry 1.036. That's a NEW position! The close order failed with reduce_only (-2022), and then it tried `开空 数量=193.100000`. But the actual filled quantity was only 11.7?\n\nHmm, 193.1 DOT @ 1.081 = $208.8 notional. That's about right for $200 notional at $1.08 price. But the exchange position shows only 11.7...\n\nWait, what if 193.1 was the close amount, and the open was separate? Let me look more carefully:\n\n```\n📝 下单详情：DOTUSDT 平仓 数量=193.100000 @ $1.081000\n🔴 DOTUSDT 主单失败，跳过 SL/TP 提交。原始响应：{'code': -2022, 'msg': 'ReduceOnly Order is rejected.'}\n⚠️ DOT reduceOnly 被币安拒（-2022），降级为普通平仓\n⚠️ DOTUSDT 设置逐仓模式失败：{'code': -4067, 'msg': 'Position side cannot be changed if there exists open orders.'}\n📝 下单详情：DOTUSDT 开空 数量=193.100000 @ $1.081000\n```\n\nSo the sequence is:\n1. Monitor tries to close DOT position with 193.1 DOT (reduce_only) → fails because exchange has 11.7\n2. Falls back to \"普通平仓\" (regular close) which opens a 193.1 DOT SHORT\n3. But there's already a DOT SHORT (the 183.2 from earlier) on the exchange, plus... hmm\n\nWait, I'm confused. Let me re-trace.\n\nBefore the close: we had DOT LONG 11.7 and DOT SHORT 183.2 on the exchange.\nAfter I ran `manual_trade.py close DOT --confirm`: it closed the DOT LONG (11.7).\n\nNow the exchange has: DOT SHORT (183.2).\n\nThen the monitor does position sync and finds:\n- Local cache says DOT position exists (from 反转重建, amount=181.0)\n- But the local cache might have been updated when we closed the LONG\n\nActually, the local cache probably still has the DOT position from before (the 反转重建 version with amount=181.0, or the one that was opened earlier). Let me check what the local cache looked like when the monitor tried to act.\n\nWait, actually after I closed the DOT LONG, the monitor probably didn't notice immediately. When the monitor then did its sync, it would:\n1. Read API: DOT amount=183.2 (SHORT) or maybe different\n2. Compare with local cache\n3. See a discrepancy\n\nBut then at 11:39:38, we see:\n```\n⚠️ DOT 恢复 Binance 止盈单失败：{'code': -2021, 'msg': 'Order would immediately trigger.'}\n```\n\nThis suggests the monitor tried to place SL/TP orders, which means it detected a position change. The SL price 1.0642 is very close to the current price (1.081), so \"Order would immediately trigger.\"\n\nThen at 11:41:36:\n```\nDOTUSDT 平仓 数量=193.100000 @ $1.081000\nreduceOnly 被币安拒（-2022），降级为普通平仓\n```\n\nSo the monitor tried to close 193.1 DOT with reduce_only but the position on exchange was only 183.2 or 11.7, so Binance rejected it.\n\nThen \"降级为普通平仓\" means it tried to open a counter-direction order (\"开空 数量=193.100000\"). This would have opened a 193.1 DOT SHORT if allowed, or netted out the existing position.\n\nBut the current position shows DOT: amount=11.7 at entry=1.036. That seems... weird. If the monitor tried to open a 193.1 DOT SHORT, how did we end up with 11.7?\n\nActually, wait. Maybe the monitor ALSO opened a LONG somewhere. Let me look for more recent DOT activity.\n\nOr maybe the DOT position I'm seeing (11.7 @ 1.036) is the RESULT of the new position that was opened. If the monitor opened a SHORT of 193.1 DOT, and there was a SHORT of 183.2 already, that would be 376.3 DOT SHORT total. But the API shows only 11.7...\n\nWait, this doesn't add up. Let me check the positions more carefully. Let me look at the full state.\n\nActually, the positions API might be returning amounts where negative = SHORT, positive = LONG. Let me check:\n- DOT: amount=11.7 → positive, so this is LONG?\n- LINK: amount=21.23 → positive, so LONG?\n\nHmm but let me also check if there's a SHORT DOT. The query I ran uses `get_all_positions()` which might only return open positions with non-zero amount. \n\nActually, looking at the binance_auto_trade code, `get_all_positions()` typically returns positions where positionAmt != 0. If the DOT SHORT of 183.2 was closed by the monitor's close attempt (which turned into a \"降级为普通平仓\"), it might have been closed.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The problem is:\n1. Monitor tried to close DOT with 193.1 reduce_only → failed\n2. \"降级为普通平仓\" → opened a regular order\n3. The regular order was \"开空 数量=193.100000\" \n\nBut wait - what if the \"降级\" logic is: instead of reduce_only close, it opens a counter position? That would mean it opened a 193.1 SHORT. But if there was already a SHORT of 183.2, it would add to it. If there was a LONG of 11.7 (which we already closed), it would net out.\n\nHmm, let me just look at this from the exchange's perspective. The current DOT position is 11.7 @ 1.036. That's a LONG position of 11.7 DOT. This means:\n- The previous DOT positions were all closed\n- A new LONG of 11.7 DOT was somehow opened\n\nWait, but the monitor log says \"开空 数量=193.100000\" (open SHORT). How did we end up with a LONG?\n\nUnless... the monitor opened a SHORT of 193.1, which closed the existing SHORT of 183.2 (by buying back), leaving a net LONG of... no that doesn't work either.\n\nOK let me take a step back and think about what might have happened:\n\n1. My close of DOT LONG (11.7) only closed the LONG position\n2. The DOT SHORT (183.2) was still there\n3. The monitor tried to manage the DOT position based on its local cache\n4. The local cache had DOT with amount=181.0 (from 反转重建)\n5. The monitor detected the position had changed direction or needed to be closed\n6. It tried to close 193.1 DOT with reduce_only → failed because the actual position was different\n7. The \"降级\" logic turned it into a MARKET order\n\nThe key issue: the MONITOR IS USING WRONG AMOUNTS (193.1 instead of actual position size). This is the same problem - the local cache doesn't match the exchange.\n\nThe actual amounts why the positions are wrong:\n- The monitor calculates the position quantity as: `200 / entry_price`\n- For DOT at ~1.08: 200/1.08 = 185 DOT\n- But the log shows 193.1, which is close enough\n- The ACTUAL filled quantity on exchange is much less\n\nWait, maybe the issue is that the monitor's local position data is stale/wrong after the manual close. The monitor didn't restart, so its local cache might think the DOT position is different from what the exchange actually has.\n\nLet me check the current positions JSON to see what the monitor thinks.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_fveYH9uOBTmTB3RTkPbk4360","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_positions.json 2>/dev/null | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null","timeout":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_A7D0LFreBGins0SlLFv16001","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"持仓同步\\|反转重建\\|DOT.*开仓\\|DOT.*方向\\|DOT.*强制重建\\|持仓数\\|get_all_positions.*个持仓\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | tail -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":985,"output":4011,"cacheRead":71424,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76420,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780544498023}}
