{"type":"message","id":"8afe8806","parentId":"9da8ced5","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:42:44.060Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the full history clearly. Let me piece together the timeline:\n\n**10:05:28** - DOT AI triggers open at 100 score, opens DOT position successfully, now 4/4 positions\n\n**10:10:17** - Position sync: local has 1 position, API has 2. \"反转重建 DOT：API原始=11.7000 → 风控标准=193.1000\"\nSo the API still shows 11.7 DOT, but the local cache corrects it to 193.1. Same bug.\n\n**11:00:18** - Hourly report: 2 positions, price cache=7\n\n**11:41:36** - Monitor tries to close DOT with 193.1 DOT reduce_only → FAILS (position is only 11.7 on exchange)\n- Falls back to \"降级为普通平仓\" → opens 193.1 DOT SHORT as regular order\n- This 193.1 SHORT closes the existing 11.7 LONG and creates a 181.4 SHORT on the exchange\n\n**11:42:06** - Position sync: API原始=181.4000 → 风控标准=185.2000\nNow the API shows 181.4 DOT SHORT (the result of the 193.1 SHORT opening that netted out with the existing LONG).\n\nSo after all of this:\n- The DOT position is now a SHORT of 181.4 DOT at entry ~1.08 → notional ~$196\n- This is ALMOST correct! (should be ~$200)\n\nWait, but earlier I queried and saw DOT: amount=11.7, entry=1.036. Let me re-query to confirm the current state.\n\nActually wait, my query was at 11:41:29, and the position sync at 11:42:06 showed API原始=181.4000. So the position changed between my query and the sync. The monitor's \"降级为普通平仓\" order at 11:41:37 opened the 193.1 SHORT, which executed and resulted in 181.4 DOT SHORT on the exchange.\n\nLet me re-query the current positions.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully:\n\nAt 11:39-11:41, the monitor was already doing SL/TP updates for DOT with stop at 1.0642 and the position sync detected the position was different (after we manually closed the LONG). Then at 11:41:36, the decision cycle triggered a close attempt:\n- It tried to close 193.1 DOT (from local cache, which was the 反转重建 value)\n- reduce_only rejected because the actual position was 11.7\n- \"降级为普通平仓\" → opened a regular sell order of 193.1 DOT SHORT\n- This 193.1 SHORT buys back the 11.7 LONG (since it was a SHORT after all...) and leaves 181.4 SHORT\n\nWait actually, that doesn't make sense. If the account already had DOT SHORT of 183.2, and the monitor opened another 193.1 SHORT... that would add to the SHORT, making it 376.3 SHORT total.\n\nUnless the DOT SHORT of 183.2 was already closed before this. Let me think again...\n\nActually, after I closed the DOT LONG (11.7), the exchange had:\n- DOT SHORT with some amount (maybe the 183.2 from earlier opened at 01:06:57)\n\nBut wait - was that 183.2 DOT SHORT still active? Let me check. The positions API at 09:01 showed only 2 positions: DOT LONG (11.7) and XRP SHORT (168.5). No DOT SHORT of 183.2. That means... the 183.2 DOT SHORT was closed at some point.\n\nActually, I now realize: at 08:39, XRP was opened as a SHORT. And at some point the DOT SHORT might have been triggered to close by stop loss or take profit.\n\nOK, this is getting complicated. Let me just focus on the user's two questions:\n1. Why only 2 positions?\n2. Why DOT only has ~1+ USDT margin?\n\nFor question 1: The system has a max of 4 positions. Currently there are 2 positions (DOT and LINK). The monitor might have had more earlier (4/4) but some were closed.\n\nFor question 2: Let me check the current DOT position state.\n\nActually, let me just re-query positions and present the current state to the user.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_8uHVw1AWLQJVSMRfYzYm3756","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nfrom binance_auto_trade import get_all_positions\npositions = get_all_positions()\nif positions:\n    for p in positions:\n        sym = p.get('symbol','?')\n        amt = p.get('amount',0)\n        entry = p.get('entry_price',0)\n        pnl = p.get('unre