{"type":"message","id":"5238a418","parentId":"9578543c","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:53:53.029Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the LINK issue now:\n\n1. LINK LONG was 21.23 on exchange, entry 7.927\n2. At 11:42:06, \"反转重建\" corrected it to 25.23 (API原始=21.2300 → 风控标准=25.2300)\n3. At 11:44, LINK TP1 hit: tried to close 25.23 @ 8.245 with reduce_only\n4. The close with 25.23 failed reduce_only (position was only 21.23 on exchange!)\n5. \"降级为普通平仓\" → opened 25.23 LINK SHORT as regular order\n6. The 25.23 SHORT netted with 21.23 LONG → leaving 4.0 LINK SHORT on exchange\n7. At 11:47:17, position sync shows \"API原始=4.0000 → 风控标准=24.3000\"\n\nSo LINK now has only 4.0 LINK SHORT on the exchange (notional ~$33), but should have ~24 LINK (~$200 notional).\n\nThe same bug happened: the close amount (25.23) was bigger than the actual position (21.23), so the reduce_only order failed, and the fallback opened a regular order that left a tiny residual position.\n\nThe root cause is the SAME as the DOT issue: the local cache amount doesn't match the exchange amount. The 反转重建 code fixes the local cache but the display uses the local amount for close orders.\n\nLet me check where the close quantity is determined. It should use the API amount, not the local cached amount.\n\nFor the other coins - the monitor shows \"开仓前检查：API 持仓=2, 本地缓存=2, 采用=2/4\" which means it thinks there are already 2 positions and has 2 slots available (out of 4). But why aren't other coins opening?\n\nLet me check: what signals are being generated? If scores are low, they won't trigger.\n\nFrom earlier, all scores were 30 (NONE). In trending market (EMA slope > 0.5%), threshold is ≥70. With scores at 30, none trigger.\n\nThe market is trending bearish, and the scoring is only giving 30 points across the board. This seems too low.\n\nBut wait - with RSI at 30-38 (oversold), the RSI component should give +35 for SHORT (since RSI < 35 is oversold, good for going SHORT). And with 24h down 5%+, the 24h change should give +25 for SHORT (since it's already down a lot, expecting continuation). That's already 60 points just from those two components!\n\nUnless the scoring is inverted for SHORT signals? Let me check the scoring logic.\n\nActually, looking at the scoring in SOUL.md:\n- RSI (35分): <35 做多 +35, >65 做空 +35\n- 24h涨跌 (25分): 跌>5% 做多 +25, 涨>5% 做空 +25\n- MA60 (20分): 价格≥MA60 做多 +20, ≤MA60 做空 +20\n\nSo the scoring is always oriented to LONG by default:\n- RSI < 35 → gives points for LONG (buy the dip)\n- 24h down >5% → gives points for LONG (buy the dip)\n- MA60 below → gives points for SHORT\n\nFor current market:\n- RSI 29-38 (all < 35, some < 35) → +35 for LONG\n- 24h -5.1% → +25 for LONG\n- Below MA60 → +20 for SHORT\n- Volume → +20 if volume is high\n\nSo if RSI is < 35, the system scores for LONG (buying the dip). This makes sense - it's a mean-reversion strategy.\n\nIf RSI > 35 but MA60 below: only +20 for SHORT + maybe volume points = max ~50.\n\nWith threshold of trending ≥70, none of these trigger!\n\nSo the issue is that the scoring system is biased toward LONG (mean reversion), and in a trending bear market with RSI at the borderline (30-38), the LONG scores aren't high enough to trigger.\n\nFor DOT, RSI=30 (below 35 threshold) → +35 LONG + 25 LONG + 0 (MA60 below, no LONG points) = 60 points. Still below 70.\n\nBut wait, the system opened DOT SHORT at 10:05 with 100 score. How? AI triggered it: `🤖 DOT 触发 AI：开仓信号确认 (100分)`. And the AI direction was \"做空(0.85%)\". So AI overrode the math scoring.\n\nOK, so the answer is:\n1. Other coins aren't opening because mathematical scores are too low (< threshold)\n2. AI can override and trigger (like DOT at 10:05 with 100 pts)\n3. LINK's amount is wrong because of the same bug: local cache amount (25.23 from reversal rebuild) ≠ exchange amount (21.23), causing close to leave residual 4.0\n\nLet me fix the LINK issue. The root problem is: when closing a position, the quantity should come from the API (actual position), NOT from the local cache. Let me find where the close quantity is calculated.\n\nActually, looking at the log more carefully:\n\n`反转重建 LINK：API原始=4.0000 → 风控标准=24.3000`\n\nAfter the failed close/fallback, the LINK position is 4.0 on exchange. The local cache corrects it to 24.3. Now if the monitor tries to close again, it'll use 24.3 instead of 4.0, causing the same problem.\n\nThis is a vicious cycle:\n1. Position on exchange: 4.0 (wrong amount)\n2. 反转重建 fixes local cache to 24.3\n3. Monitor tries to close: uses 24.3 from local cache → fails reduce_only → fallback opens 24.3 counter position\n4. Result: actual position becomes ~20.3 on the opposite side (if it was SHORT 4.0, + buy 24.3 = net LONG 20.3)\n5. Cycle repeats\n\nThe fix needs to be: close positions using the API amount, not the local cached amount. OR: the local cache should store the API amount.\n\nLet me look at how the close is triggered and find the quantity source.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_T03E5pqovYnydEksszD45087","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"def.*close\\|平仓.*数量\\|close.*qty\\|close.*amount\\|position_amount\\|close_position\\|reduce_only\" /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py 2>/dev/null | head -30","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1219,"output":2932,"cacheRead":83968,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88119,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780545200466}}
