 10) / entry\n```\n\nFor DOT entry=1.02: expected_qty = 200/1.02 = 196 DOT. But the API shows 11.7.\n\nSo either:\n1. The open order had a wrong calculation\n2. The position on the exchange was set incorrectly (not by our code)\n3. There's a precision/rounding issue\n\nLet me check: what if `format_quantity` for DOT is capping the quantity? DOT has 1 decimal precision according to SOUL.md. 196.1 DOT should be fine.\n\nWhat if the monitor never actually opened this position? What if this is the same old 11.7 DOT position that somehow never got closed? Let me check the timeline...\n\nAfter the 12:02 restart, the monitor should have opened fresh positions. Let me check the log for DOT opens after restart.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_B3dDtqqO3HbXJELQY7N16447","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"DOT.*开\\|DOT.*下单\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | grep \"2026-06-04 12:\\|2026-06-04 13:\\|2026-06-04 14:\\|2026-06-04 15:\\|2026-06-04 16:\\|2026-06-04 17:\\|2026-06-04 18:\\|2026-06-04 19:\" | head -20","timeout":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_L7wegLnbOOJsfh7oVytx4483","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_positions.json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\npositions=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor p in positions:\n    sym=p['symbol']\n    amt=p.get('amount',p.get('qty',0))\n    entry=p.get('entry_price',0)\n    tp=p.get('type','?')\n    notional=amt*float(entry)\n    print(f'{sym}: {tp}, {amt}个 @ \\${entry}, 名义\\${notional:.0f}')\n\"","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":206,"output":1791,"cacheRead":104576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":106573,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780573941504}}
