{"type":"message","id":"bda52747","parentId":"152700c7","timestamp":"2026-06-04T11:54:03.641Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no DOT close event between 17:00 and 17:45! The position just changed direction without any log. This means the SL Algo order triggered on the exchange side directly (not via monitor code). The Algo order at around 1.03 triggered a market buy that closed the SHORT.\n\nWait, but Algo orders on Binance close positions. If the SL triggered, it would close the SHORT, leaving zero position. How would it then become LONG 11.7?\n\nUnless... the TP Algo order or a stop-market order had some other effect. Or maybe there was an exchange-side issue.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The SL for the SHORT was at 1.03 (above entry). When price hit 1.03, the Algo triggered a buy order to close the SHORT. But the position became LONG. \n\nIn Binance hedge mode, a stop-market order for a SHORT triggers a BUY. If the buy quantity is larger than the SHORT position, it could flip to LONG. But the Algo should be \"close position\" type, not \"open position\".\n\nOR: maybe the Algo SL closed the position, and then the monitor detected the direction change and did something that opened a LONG.\n\nWait, looking at the 17:45 log:\n```\n🔄 持仓同步：DOT 方向变化 SHORT→LONG，强制重建\n```\n\nThe \"强制重建\" (forced rebuild) just creates new positions in the local cache. It doesn't open positions on the exchange. So the exchange already had a LONG position at 17:45.\n\nSo between 17:00 and 17:45:\n1. DOT SHORT SL triggered on the exchange (price went above 1.03)\n2. The SL Algo closed the SHORT\n3. Something then opened a LONG of 11.7 DOT\n\nBut the monitor didn't open a LONG in the log! Let me search for when the LONG was opened.\n\nActually, maybe I should look before 17:00. Maybe the SL triggered earlier and the LONG was opened earlier.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_byyBWZXdvnYGrOfiR4mJ9386","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"DOT\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | grep \"2026-06-04 1[56]:\" | grep -i \"开多\\|LONG.*开\\|BUY\\|平仓\\|close\\|SL触发\\|TP触发\\|止损触发\\|止盈触发\" | head -15","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":102,"output":1017,"cacheRead":111488,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":112607,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780574029946}}
{"type":"message","id":"43e193b3","parentId":"bda52747","timestamp":"2026-06-04T11:54:03.786Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_byyBWZXdvnYGrOfiR4mJ9386","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2026-06-04 15:24:33 [INFO] 📝 下单结果：{'leverage': {'symbol': 'DOTUSDT', 'leverage': 10, 'maxNotionalValue': '1000000'}, 'order': {'orderId': 234421844, 'symbol': 'DOTUSDT', 'status': 'NEW', 'clientOrderId': 'oc_1780557869_8f7c1fb24a', 'price': '0.000', 'avgPrice': '0.00', 'origQty': '191.0', 'executedQty': '0.0', 'cumQty': '0.0', 'cumQuote': '0.0000', 'timeInForce': 'GTC', 'type': 'MARKET', 'reduceOnly': False, 'closePosition': False, 'side': 'SELL', 'positionSide': 'BOTH', 'stopPrice': '0.000', 'workingType': 'CONTRACT_PRICE', 'priceProtect': False, 'origType': 'MARKET', 'priceMatch': 'NONE', 'selfTradePreventionMode': 'EXPIRE_MAKER', 'goodTillDate': 0, 'updateTime': 1780557872075}, 'quantity_used': 191.0, 'tp_price': 1.01, 'sl_price': 1.07, 'success': True, 'message': ''}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":118,"aggregated":"2026-06-04 15:24:33 [INFO] 📝 下单结果：{'leverage': {'symbol': 'DOTUSDT', 'leverage': 10, 'maxNotionalValue': '1000000'}, 'order': {'orderId': 234421844, 'symbol': 'DOTUSDT', 'status': 'NEW', 'clientOrderId': 'oc_1780557869_8f7c1fb24a', 'price': '0.000', 'avgPrice': '0.00', 'origQty': '191.0', 'executedQty': '0.0', 'cumQty': '0.0', 'cumQuote': '0.0000', 'timeInForce': 'GTC', 'type': 'MARKET', 'reduceOnly': False, 'closePosition': False, 'side': 'SELL', 'positionSide': 'BOTH', 'stopPrice': '0.000', 'workingType': 'CONTRACT_PRICE', 'priceProtect': False, 'origType': 'MARKET', 'priceMatch': 'NONE', 'selfTradePreventionMode': 'EXPIRE_MAKER', 'goodTillDate': 0, 'updateTime': 1780557872075}, 'quantity_used': 191.0, 'tp_price': 1.01, 'sl_price': 1.07, 'success': True, 'message': ''}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780574043778}}
{"type":"message","id":"e1de5cd3","parentId":"43e193b3","timestamp":"2026-06-04T11:54:32.543Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No close events for this DOT SHORT at all. The position went from SHORT 191.0 at 17:00 to LONG 11.7 at 17:45 without any log of closing or opening.\n\nThis is very suspicious. The likely explanation:\n1. The DOT SL Algo triggered on the exchange\n2. The Algo order closed the position, but then the exchange had some residual or a ghost position\n3. The monitor detected the direction change and did a forced rebuild\n\nBut why 11.7? This exact number keeps showing up. It seems like the exchange is somehow creating 11.7 DOT positions instead of the full amount.\n\nWait, let me check the position history more carefully. Maybe the monitor IS opening positions correctly but the exchange is not filling them fully:\n\nAt 15:24: open DOT SHORT with 191.0 quantity\n- This is a MARKET order for SELL 191.0 DOT\n- status: NEW, origQty: 191.0, executedQty: 0.0 (not filled yet)\n\nThe order is NEW with 0 executed. It should fill on the market. But what if it didn't fill completely?\n\nActually, MARKET orders should fill immediately. The status going from NEW to FILLED happens on the exchange. Our code only gets the initial response back (status: NEW) and then later the order fills.\n\nLet me check if maybe the 191.0 SELL order partially filled. With DOT price ~$1.05 and 191 DOT = ~$200 notional, that's well within the testnet limits. There shouldn't be a partial fill issue.\n\nOK, let me take a completely different approach. Let me look at how the position sync/rebuild works and what happens when it detects a direction change.\n\nAt 17:45:41:\n```\n🔄 持仓同步：DOT 方向变化 SHORT→LONG，强制重建\n🔧 反转重建 DOT：API原始=11.7000 → 风控标准=196.7000\n```\n\nThe API shows 11.7 DOT LONG position. The local cache was tracking a SHORT. This mismatch triggers a rebuild.\n\nThe rebuild code (line 2342+):\n```python\nfor p in api_positions:\n    amt = float(p.get('amount', 0))\n    if amt != 0:\n        entry = float(p.get('entry_price', 0))\n        expected_qty = (CONFIG[\"total_capital\"] * size_pct * 10) / entry\n        correct_amount = format_quantity(symbol, expected_qty, entry)\n        new_positions.append({\n            'amount': correct_amount,  # 196.7\n            ...\n        })\n```\n\nSo after rebuild, local cache has DOT LONG, amount=196.7. But the EXCHANGE still has only 11.7.\n\nThis means the monitor's local cache is correct (196.7) but the actual exchange position is WRONG (11.7).\n\nThe root question remains: WHY does the exchange position keep ending up at 11.7 DOT?\n\nHypothesis: Maybe the monitor ISN'T the one opening these 11.7 DOT positions. Maybe there's something else creating them. Or maybe the open orders are being placed but partially filling.\n\nLet me verify: when the monitor opens DOT, what quantity does it actually submit?\n\nFrom the 15:24 log: origQty='191.0', executedQty='0.0' (this is just the initial NEW state). The order should fill to 191.0.\n\nBut the HEDGE MODE behavior on Binance: when you have no position and submit a SELL order, it opens a SHORT position. In BOTH mode, this should just work.\n\nLet me look at the LINK issue too. LINK opened at some point after restart. Let me find when.\n\nActually, let me step back and think about this more systematically.\n\nThe problem patterns:\n1. DOT: exchange shows 11.7 when it should be ~191-197\n2. LINK: exchange shows 21.23 when it should be ~24-25\n3. BNB and BTC are close to expected\n\nDOT 11.7 came from the old buggy position that we've been chasing all day. Each time we close it and the monitor opens a new one, it somehow ends up as 11.7 again.\n\nLINK 21.23 - this is close to the corrected amount. But the local cache says 25.23. So LINK might be a similar pattern but with a smaller discrepancy.\n\nActually wait - LINK 21.23 could be from the LAST recon where the monitor opened a position and the exchange filled it to 21.23. The local cache was then corrected to 25.23 by 反转重建. So the local cache is ahead of the exchange.\n\nThe fundamental question: are positions opening with wrong quantities, or are they opening correctly and then being reduced by something?\n\nLet me check if maybe the Binance testnet has a bug where MARKET orders don't fill completely. Or maybe there's a position precision/rounding issue.\n\nDOT has precision 1 (according to SOUL.md: \"DOT: 1位\"). So 196.7 should round to 196.7. That's fine.\n\nLet me check the format_quantity function.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_X7duBizBfbxBvqAcAHy27268","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"def format_quantity\\|PRECISION\\|step_size\\|lot_size\\|min_qty\\|tick_size\\|DOT.*precision\\|DOT.*step\" /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py 2>/dev/null | head -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":368,"output":2368,"cacheRead":112128,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":114864,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780574043798}}
