{"type":"message","id":"2daa8a95","parentId":"4f7a2cc4","timestamp":"2026-06-04T11:54:41.350Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_bf8jE4ADmeVaWByAlJyZ9036","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    precision_map = {\n        'BTC': 3,      # stepSize: 0.001\n        'ETH': 3,      # stepSize: 0.001\n        'SOL': 2,      # stepSize: 0.01\n        'BNB': 2,      # stepSize: 0.01 ✅ 2026-03-28 修复：3→2 位\n        'DOT': 1,      # stepSize: 0.1\n        'LINK': 2,     # stepSize: 0.01\n        'XRP': 1,      # stepSize: 0.1 ✅ 2026-03-31 同步：加回 XRP\n    }\n    \n    return precision_map.get(symbol.upper(), 8)  # 默认 8 位\n\ndef format_quantity(symbol, quantity, price):\n    \"\"\"格式化数量到正确的精度（Binance 要求 8 位小数）\"\"\"\n    precision = get_quantity_precision(symbol, price)\n    \n    # 简单 round 到正确精度\n    # 修复：XRP 精度 1 位，8.5/2=4.25 → 4.2（向下兼容）\n    return round(quantity, precision)\n\ndef format_price(price):\n    \"\"\"格式化价格到正确的精度\"\"\"\n    if price >= 1000:\n        return round(price, 2)\n    elif price >= 100:\n        return round(price, 2)\n    elif price >= 10:\n        return round(price, 2)\n    elif price >= 1:\n        return round(price, 2)\n    elif price >= 0.1:\n        return round(price, 4)\n    elif price >= 0.01:\n        return round(price, 5)\n    else:\n        return round(price, 6)\n\ndef set_isolated_margin(symbol):\n    \"\"\"\n    设置逐仓模式 (ISOLATED)\n\n[284 more lines in file. Use offset=300 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780574081337}}
{"type":"message","id":"992004e5","parentId":"2daa8a95","timestamp":"2026-06-04T11:55:08.789Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, the precision is correct. For DOT at ~$1:\n- quantity = round(200/1.02, 1) = round(196.08, 1) = 196.1\n- Or with exact price 1.047: quantity = round(200/1.047, 1) = round(190.07, 1) = 190.1\n\nActually, the 15:24 order used origQty=191.0. Let me check: 200/1.047 = 191.02, round to 1 decimal = 191.0. That matches!\n\nSo the order quantity is correct (191.0). The issue is why the position ends up at 11.7 instead of 191.0.\n\nLet me think about this differently. In BOTH mode on Binance Futures, when you have an existing position and open a trade in the opposite direction, the positions net out. \n\nWhat if the monitor's close_position function didn't actually close the old DOT SHORT, and then the new open netted with it?\n\nNo wait - the DOT SHORT was closed at 13:35 (SL close, +2.13%). After that, there should be no DOT position.\n\nThen at 15:24, DOT SHORT 191.0 is opened. The exchange should now have a SHORT of 191.0 DOT.\n\nBut at 17:45, the exchange shows LONG 11.7. This means:\n1. DOT SHORT was closed (SL triggered)\n2. Something created a LONG 11.7\n\nThe SL Algo triggering is handled by Binance - the monitor doesn't log it if it's a server-side Algo order. So the Algo SL closed the position, but then how did the LONG appear?\n\nMaybe the monitor detected the position was closed and then opened a new position? But I don't see any open log between 15:24 and 17:45 for DOT.\n\nActually, wait. Let me search for DOT opens after 17:00.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_rgGH1MZLsga1u0HgB5WH7703","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"DOT.*开\\|DOT.*下单\\|开空 DOT\\|开多 DOT\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | grep \"2026-06-04 17:\" | head -10","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage"