{"type":"message","id":"8a81d5b8","parentId":"2768c596","timestamp":"2026-06-04T11:57:56.738Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There it is! The second order (17:42:39) has:\n- qty=202.7\n- type=MARKET\n- reduce=True (reduceOnly)\n- closePos=True\n- status=FILLED\n\nBut it's a REGULAR MARKET order, not a conditional Algo order. It has orderId=234467915 which is a regular order ID, not an algoId.\n\nThis means the monitor's close_position function was called to close the DOT SHORT, and it submitted a MARKET order with reduceOnly=True, quantity=202.7.\n\nBut wait, earlier I looked at the monitor logs and there was no close event logged for DOT between 15:25 and 17:45. Let me search again more carefully.\n\nActually, the BUY order at 17:42:39 is a MARKET order with closePos=True and reduce=True. This looks like a REGULAR close order placed by the monitor's close_position function, not an Algo order.\n\nLet me re-check: how was this order submitted? The order has qty=202.7, which means the close_position() used qty=202.7.\n\nWhere did 202.7 come from? Remember the local cache has amount=196.7 (from 反转重建). 202.7 is close to 196.7 but not exact.\n\nActually, 202.7 looks like it could be: round(200 / algo_trigger_price, 1) = round(200 / some_price, 1).\n\nHmm, let me search the monitor log for a close event. Maybe it was logged differently than I expected.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_zFEZuliym5dCkWov0ZKs3298","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"DOT.*平\\|DOT.*close\\|DOT.*reduce\\|17:42\\|orderId.*234467915\\|平仓 DOT\\|DOT 平仓\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | grep \"2026-06-04 17:\" | head -15","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":216,"output":805,"cacheRead":115456,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":116477,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUs