qty, entry)\n                            log.info(f\"🔧 反转重建 {symbol}：API原始={abs(amt):.4f} → 风控标准={correct_amount:.4f}\")\n                            # 重建止盈止损字段（使用统一 calc_tp_sl，防止 KeyError）\n                            tp_sl = calc_tp_sl(entry, 'LONG' if amt > 0 else 'SHORT', {}, {})\n                            tp1 = tp_sl['tp1_price']\n                            sl = tp_sl['sl_price']\n                            new_positions.append({\n                                'symbol': symbol,\n                                'type': 'SHORT' if amt < 0 else 'LONG',\n                                'entry_price': entry,\n                                'amount': correct_amount,\n                                'tp1_price': tp1,\n                                'tp2_price': 0.0,  # 已废弃，全在 TP1 全平\n                                'sl_price': sl,\n                                'tp1_hit': False,\n                                'size_remaining': 1.0,\n                            })\n                    positions = new_positions\n                    save_positions(positions)\n                    log.info(f\"✅ 持仓同步完成：{len(positions)}个\")\n                    # 🐛 仓位反转修复：重建后提交止盈止损 Algo 单\n                    for pos in positions:\n                        submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)\n            except Exception as e:\n                log.error(f\"⚠️ 同步失败：{e}\")\n\n        try:\n            # ──────────────────────────────────\n            # Step 1: 获取实时价格（0 REST请求）\n            # ──────────────────────────────────\n            prices = {sym: price_stream.get(sym) for sym in CONFIG[\"symbols\"]}\n\n            # ──────────────────────────────────\n            # Step 2: 止盈止损检查（每15秒，最轻量）\n            # ──────────────────────────────────\n            exits = check_exits_fast(positions, prices)\n            for pos, reason, size in exits:\n                p = prices[pos[\"symbol\"]][\"price\"]\n                pnl = close_position(pos, reason, size, p)\n                circuit_breaker.record_trade(pnl)\n\n                # 🐛 2026-06-03 修复：平仓后验证 API 才删除本地持仓，防止平仓失败时被 API 同步救回循环\n                if reason == \"TP1\":\n                    positions.remove(pos)\n                    save_positions(positions)\n                    log.info(f\"TP1 触发 {pos['symbol']}，全平移除\")\n                elif reason == \"SL\":\n                    # 先同步 API 确认仓位真的没了再删\n                    sym_closed = pos['symbol']\n                    positions.remove(pos)\n\n[266 more lines in file. Use offset=2420 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780574671714}}
{"type":"message","id":"c5083ab7","parentId":"fbd4a0a0","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:05:03.935Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the problem more clearly. In the rebuild flow (lines 2360-2392), positions are rebuilt with `correct_amount` from the formula (e.g., 196.7 for DOT). Then at line 2392, `submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)` is called with the REBUILT position that has `amount=196.7`.\n\nIf we pass this quantity to the Algo order, the Algo will try to submit with qty=196.7, but the actual exchange position is only 11.7. The Algo might fail because the quantity exceeds the position, OR it might behave unexpectedly.\n\nBut wait - the exchange position IS 11.7 after rebuild, and the Algo order would say \"close 196.7\" which doesn't exist. The Algo order might:\n1. Reject because quantity > position\n2. Close only 11.7 (since that's all there is)\n\nActually, for closePosition=true, Binance auto-calculates and got 202.7 instead of 191.0. That was wrong. But if we pass 11.7 (the actual position), it should work correctly.\n\nSo the fix should be: in `submit_initial_algo_orders`, use the ACTUAL exchange position amount (`abs(amt)` from API), not the corrected amount. But the function only receives `pos` which has the corrected amount.\n\nHmm, this is getting complicated. Let me think about the cleanest approach.\n\nThe key insight: the Algo order quantity should ALWAYS match what's actually on the exchange. It doesn't matter what the local cache says.\n\nOptions:\nA. Pass the API position amount to `submit_initial_algo_orders` as well\nB. Have `submit_initial_algo_orders` use `pos[\"amount\"]` but trust that the Algo will handle partial closes\nC. Use `closePosition=true` BUT also add `quantity` to constrain it\n\nActually, the simplest and safest fix that addresses the root cause without creating new issues:\n\n1. **For `place_algo_conditional_order`**: Replace `closePosition=true` with explicit `quantity`\n2. **For `submit_initial_algo_orders` (rebuild context)**: Pass the actual API position size from the caller\n3. **For `sync_stop_loss_to_binance`** (SL update during position lifecycle): Also use the position's actual exchange quantity\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The issue with `closePosition=true` is that when the SL/TP triggered, the exchange calculated 202.7 instead of 191.0. If we pass quantity=191.0, the Algo should submit a MARKET order for exactly 191.0 when triggered.\n\nBut in the rebuild case (line 2392), the rebuilt position has amount=196.7 (corrected), while the exchange has 11.7. If we call `submit_initial_algo_orders` with qty=196.7 but the exchange only has 11.7, the Algo might:\n- Fail/reject\n- Close only 11.7 (which is correct behavior since that's the actual position)\n\nActually, looking at line 2360-2392 more carefully:\n```python\nnew_positions.append({\n    'amount': correct_amount,  # 196.7\n    ...\n})\n...\nfor pos in positions:\n    submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)\n```\n\nThe problem is that `correct_amount` (196.7) is different from the actual exchange amount (11.7). But we want the Algo to cover the actual position (11.7), not the corrected amount.\n\nSo the fix needs to be:\n1. `submit_initial_algo_orders` should use the ACTUAL exchange position amount\n2. But the function only knows what `pos` tells it, and `pos[\"amount\"]` is the corrected value\n\nThe cleanest fix: in the rebuild loop, pass the actual API amount to `submit_initial_algo_orders`, or modify `submit_initial_algo_orders` to query the exchange for the actual position.\n\nActually, the simplest approach: modify `submit_initial_algo_orders` to receive an optional `api_amount` parameter. If provided, use that; otherwise use `pos[\"amount\"]`.\n\nOr even simpler: just query the API in `submit_initial_algo_orders` to get the actual position. But that adds an API call.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole approach. The simplest thing that fixes the root cause:\n\n1. Modify `place_algo_conditional_order()` to accept `quantity` parameter. If provided, use `quantity` and `reduceOnly=true` instead of `closePosition=true`.\n2. Modify `submit_initial_algo_orders()` and `sync_stop_loss_to_binance()` to pass the position quantity from `pos[\"amount\"]`.\n\nBUT in the rebuild case, `pos[\"amount\"]` is 196.7 while the exchange has 11.7. If the Algo is set to close 196.7 but the position is only 11.7, what happens?\n\nOn Binance, a `reduceOnly` order with quantity > position will close the entire position. So qty=196.7 on an 11.7 LONG would just close 11.7. That's SAFE - it won't flip to the other side.\n\nWait, is that actually true? Let me double-check. In Binance Futures, a `reduceOnly` order:\n- If quantity > position, it will reduce by the position amount (closes position)\n- If quantity < position, it will partially close\n\nSo passing qty=196.7 to close an 11.7 position would just close 11.7. Safe!\n\nBut there's another consideration: what if the Algo order can't be placed because the quantity format is wrong? DOT has precision 1, so 196.7 is valid. The Algo would be placed with qty=196.7 but when triggered, it would only close 11.7 (the actual position).\n\nThis should work. Let me proceed with the fix.\n\nPlan:\n1. `binance_auto_trade.py`: `place_algo_conditional_order()` → add `quantity=None` param. If provided, use `quantity` + `reduceOnly=true` instead of `closePosition=true`\n2. `crypto_signal_monitor.py`: All callers pass the position quantity\n   - `sync_stop_loss_to_binance()` → needs quantity parameter added\n   - `submit_initial_algo_orders()` → uses `pos[\"amount\"]`\n   - Callers of `sync_stop_loss_to_binance()` at lines 698, 711, 718 → need to pass quantity from `pos`\n\nLet me also check the callers at lines 698, 711, 718.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_OZfkvO97HNJHHwC5fSza3682","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","limit":35