successfully at 1.0577. The SL should have been submitted with its price. The SL price is likely something like 0.97 or thereabouts (below the LONG entry).\n\nLet me check the SL price. If the SL is 0.981 for example, `format_price(0.981)` → 0.981 < 1, so it uses `round(0.981, 4)` = 0.981. That should be fine for DOT which has price precision 4.\n\nActually, I bet the issue is something else entirely. Let me just look at what price was sent for the SL.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_wiCyXhgutHsTsYdPeZoS1348","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"2026-06-04 20:16\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | head -10","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":326,"output":3614,"cacheRead":66432,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":70372,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780575415675}}
