{"type":"message","id":"fcaf26f2","parentId":"39a94724","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:19:40.890Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK the exchange info is way too long. The DOT precision from the exchange info shows DOT has different PRICE_FILTER entries for different contract types. Looking at the ones that match DOT price ~$1:\n\nFor DOT price at ~$1: tickSize could be 0.0001, 0.00001, or 0.001 depending on the contract type. But these are all sub-contracts/perpetual futures for different pairs.\n\nThe key issue: the error -1111 happened for the SL Algo but NOT the TP Algo. Both use the same quantity and the same code path. The difference must be the triggerPrice.\n\nSL was for a LONG, so SL is below entry (1.02) → maybe ~0.98. The `format_price(0.98)` would use `round(0.98, 4)` = 0.98. That should be fine for tickSize 0.0001.\n\nTP was at 1.0577 (from the success log). `format_price(1.0577)` = 1.0577. That's 4 decimal places. Also fine for tickSize 0.0001.\n\nI'm stuck on what caused the -1111. But my earlier tests showed that explicit quantity works fine with DOTUSDT for both 11.7, 196.1, and 196.7. The issue was something specific to the startup flow.\n\nWait - the error code is -1111 which is \"Precision is over the maximum defined for this asset\". Maybe it's not about DOT at all! Maybe it's about the TRIGGER PRICE formatting for an Algo order. \n\nLet me think... when submitting with closePosition=true, Binance doesn't need quantity. When I switched to quantity-based, maybe something changed in how Binance validates the order.\n\nBut the TP with quantity succeeded! So quantity + DOT works.\n\nHmm, maybe the error was from BEFORE my code change was effective. The monitor startup loads the saved crypto_positions.json which was saved from BEFORE the restart. If the old code path was used somehow...\n\nActually, wait - I compiled the files and they passed. The restart should use the new code. Let me check if the monitor log after the error shows any more activity - is it still running and processing normally?\n\nLet me check more recent logs to see if the monitor recovered.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_DPqNaS1jzwRJJnT1gLYi1357","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"tail -15 /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"价格流\\|WebSocket\\|缓存\\|score\\|每分钟\"","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":96910,"output":1088,"cacheRead":18688,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":116686,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780575564127}}
